* amplikt88 SPICE models for ngspice (KiCad 10)
* Valves: Koren models fitted to the data sheets in docs/datasheets.
* ECC83: Philips anode curves (Vg 0 to -4 V, 0.15 to 3.75 mA), 10 % rms; it gives the
*   typical points (100 V, -1 V: 0.50 mA, 1.25 mA/V; 250 V, -2 V: 1.17 mA, 1.68 mA/V, 60k).
* ECC81: Philips anode curves (Vg 0 to -8 V, 0.75 to 18 mA), 5 % rms; typical points
*   within about 10 % (250 V, -2 V: 9.8 mA, 5.2 mA/V, 12k).
* KT88: JJ plate curves at Vg2 = 300 V (Va 40 to 450 V, knee included) and the Genalex
*   typical points (tetrode 250 V, -15 V: 136 mA; ultralinear 453 V, -59 V: 47 mA;
*   553 V, -75 V: 55 mA), 12 % rms; about 10 % low at the knee with the grid near 0 V,
*   which is where maximum power is decided. Screen current about 3 % of the anode
*   current; the model does not raise it at low anode voltage, so it understates Ig2
*   on signal peaks.
* No contact potential and no grid current below 0 V. Use results to compare, not to certify.

.model DGRID D(IS=1n RS=1 CJO=0.5p TT=1n)

* Koren triode. Pins: A G K
.subckt TRIODE A G K MU=112.4 EX=1.1 KG1=813 KP=623 KVB=10670 RGI=2k CGK=2.3p CGP=1.7p CPK=0.9p
RG G GI {RGI}
DG GI K DGRID
BE1 E1 0 V = V(A,K)/KP*ln(1+exp(KP*(1/MU+V(GI,K)/sqrt(KVB+V(A,K)*V(A,K)))))
BIP A K I = u(V(E1))*2*pwr(abs(V(E1)),EX)/KG1
CGK GI K {CGK}
CGP GI A {CGP}
CPK A K {CPK}
RE1 E1 0 1e9
.ends TRIODE

* Dual triode 12AX7 / ECC83. Pins follow the noval socket: A1 G1 K1 A2 G2 K2
.subckt ECC83 A1 G1 K1 A2 G2 K2
X1 A1 G1 K1 TRIODE MU=112.4 EX=1.1 KG1=813 KP=623 KVB=10670 CGK=1.6p CGP=1.7p CPK=0.46p
X2 A2 G2 K2 TRIODE MU=112.4 EX=1.1 KG1=813 KP=623 KVB=10670 CGK=1.6p CGP=1.7p CPK=0.46p
.ends ECC83

* Dual triode 12AU7 / ECC82
.subckt ECC82 A1 G1 K1 A2 G2 K2
X1 A1 G1 K1 TRIODE MU=21.5 EX=1.3 KG1=1180 KP=84 KVB=300 CGK=1.6p CGP=1.5p CPK=0.5p
X2 A2 G2 K2 TRIODE MU=21.5 EX=1.3 KG1=1180 KP=84 KVB=300 CGK=1.6p CGP=1.5p CPK=0.5p
.ends ECC82

* Dual triode 12AT7 / ECC81
.subckt ECC81 A1 G1 K1 A2 G2 K2
X1 A1 G1 K1 TRIODE MU=80.7 EX=1.05 KG1=299 KP=246 KVB=4190 CGK=2.3p CGP=1.6p CPK=0.2p
X2 A2 G2 K2 TRIODE MU=80.7 EX=1.05 KG1=299 KP=246 KVB=4190 CGK=2.3p CGP=1.6p CPK=0.2p
.ends ECC81

* Koren pentode / beam tetrode, with a tanh knee and a linear slope (KVA) in place of
* Koren's atan, which is too soft for the KT88. Pins: A G2 G1 K
.subckt PENTODE A G2 G1 K MU=8 EX=1.35 KG1=1000 KG2=8000 KP=32 KVB=16 KVA=1000 RGI=1k CGK=14p CGP=0.8p CPK=8p
RG G1 GI {RGI}
DG GI K DGRID
BE1 E1 0 V = max(V(G2,K),1)/KP*ln(1+exp(KP*(1/MU+V(GI,K)/max(V(G2,K),1))))
BIA A K I = u(V(E1))*2*pwr(abs(V(E1)),EX)/KG1*tanh(max(V(A,K),0)/KVB)*(1+max(V(A,K),0)/KVA)
BIG G2 K I = u(V(E1))*2*pwr(abs(V(E1)),EX)/KG2
CGK GI K {CGK}
CGP GI A {CGP}
CPK A K {CPK}
RE1 E1 0 1e9
.ends PENTODE

* KT88 (beam tetrode). Pins follow the symbol: A G2 G1 K
.subckt KT88 A G2 G1 K
X1 A G2 G1 K PENTODE MU=7.63 EX=1.592 KG1=2008 KG2=41000 KP=39.0 KVB=49.2 KVA=703
.ends KT88

* Trimmer: pins 1 2(wiper) 3, POS is the wiper position from pin 1 (0..1)
.subckt POT_TRIM 1 2 3 R=10k POS=0.5
R12 1 2 {R*POS+1m}
R23 2 3 {R*(1-POS)+1m}
.ends POT_TRIM

* Push-pull ultralinear output transformer.
* Pins: A1 UL1 CT UL2 A2 SHI SLO. Taps at 40% of each half from CT.
* LH = inductance of one primary half, RATIO = total primary : secondary turns,
* KC = coupling (leakage = 4*LH*(1-KC^2) seen from the whole primary), RP = resistance of one half,
* CW = shunt capacitance anode to anode.
.subckt OT_PP_UL A1 UL1 CT UL2 A2 SHI SLO LH=10 RATIO=22.4 KC=0.9997 RP=60 RS=0.3 CW=300p
RPA A1 NA {RP*0.6}
LA NA UL1 {LH*0.36}
RPB UL1 NB {RP*0.4}
LB NB CT {LH*0.16}
RPC CT NC {RP*0.4}
LC NC UL2 {LH*0.16}
RPD UL2 ND {RP*0.6}
LD ND A2 {LH*0.36}
LS SHI NS {4*LH/(RATIO*RATIO)}
RSS NS SLO {RS}
CWP A1 A2 {CW}
KAB LA LB {KC}
KAC LA LC {KC}
KAD LA LD {KC}
KAS LA LS {KC}
KBC LB LC {KC}
KBD LB LD {KC}
KBS LB LS {KC}
KCD LC LD {KC}
KCS LC LS {KC}
KDS LD LS {KC}
.ends OT_PP_UL
